  "description": "Change of use of first, second and third floors from Class E to Class C3, creating two residential apartments, replacement of glass panels with solid wood on the Albion Street entrance door and replacement of lightwell condenser units, installation of one air source heat pump in basement lightwell and two air source heat pumps in lightwell vaults and internal alterations, including the reopening of a small portion of the ground-floor party wall between 23 Albion Street and 61 Connaught Street to connect the commercial units; changes to the plan form, including the creation of a new residential entrance hall and corridor from Albion Street, incorporating a service riser cupboard; refurbishment, repair, reinstatement and reconfiguration of the basement, ground, first, second and third floors to facilitate residential use of the upper floors; formation of a raised floor and suspended ceiling within the first-floor bathroom; formation of small-scale service penetrations through existing walls (approximately 50mm in diameter) to accommodate pipework; and alterations to the vaults to create four new openings in the wall to accommodate the housing of air source heat pumps within two vaults, external alterations, including the remodelling of a secondary door on Albion Street to reinstate historic features, replacement of one modern window, and minor repairs to the render and brickwork, including repointing, to the Albion Street and Connaught Street elevations. (Linked to 26/04304/LBC)",
